WINDOWS

Introduction:
I find the best way to think about this project is as 2 seperate servers 
- a backend server that acts as an API containing all business logic and serves this to path endpoints
- a frontend server that the user will interact with, this has the nice looking html/css/js and will communicate with our backend API to fetch business logic
This means we need to set up each server differently, in the github I have separated each one into a different server (frontend/backend) for readability, this guide will take 
you through cloning the github, installing dependencies and how to run the servers locally. At the end it will also explain how to develop properly
e.g: when to git fetch and git pull and how to test locally

STEP 1:
  Clone Repository (Prerequisites: Git)
  
  1) open VS Code
  2) Clone repository with the following command
  > git clone https://github.com/JamesAlexanderC/Project-Ate.git
  3) fill out your GitHub username + password for verification when prompted
  4) reopen vs code inside the folder that has been made

STEP 2:
  Django backend setup (Prerequisites: Python 3.11)
  
  Step 0, 0.1 and 0.2 show you how to set up and use a virtual environment (provides a dedicated python interpreter and packages you install on it are isolated to the venv),
  these steps are fully optional and down to preference, if you follow them make sure you activate and deactivate the venv as directed to avoid errors and version conflicts.
  
  0) Set up python virtual environment for Django backend framework and libraries with the following command 
  > python -m venv venv
  0.1) Activate the environemnt when you are working on the Django backend with the following command (must be run from the project root folder) 
  > venv\Scripts\activate
  0.2) Deactivate the environment when you finish or when you start working on the React frontend with the following command
  > deactivate
  
  1) Navigate into backend directory with the following command
  > cd backend
  2) Install the backend requirements with the following command
  > pip install -r requirements.txt
  3) Create the SQLite database with the following command
  > python manage.py migrate
  4) Verify the environment is working by running the server with the following command
  > python manage.py runserver
  5) This should have run the backend server, access it by visiting 'http://127.0.0.1:8000/' in your browser
  6) Close the server on the command line (Ctrl+C)
  7) Create a new user so you can access the built in admin panel with the following command
  > python manage.py createsuperuser
  8) Make the username and password whatever you want, you can leave the email blank
  9) Now run the server again as directed in step 4
  10) Access admin panel by visiting 'http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/' in your browser,
  from here you can easily edit the database. Note: changes to the DB are never stored in github
  **This is a development server, never expose it to a public port**

STEP 3:
  React frontend setup (Prerequisites: None)
  
  You can follow this part in a seperate window or the same window as the last part, 
  if you want to run the backend and frontend together, you will have to run them both from different windows,
  if you are following this part in the same window as the last part make sure your virtual environment (if you have one) is deactivated,
  if you are following this part in a different window, make sure it's opened to the same directory as the previous one (Project-Ate)
  
  1) Visit 'https://nodejs.org/en/download' and download the windows msi installer
  2) Run the installer, and make sure to check 'add to path'
  ) if you are using the same window as you were previously navigate back to the root directory with following command
  > cd ..
  3) Navigate into frontend directory with the following command
  > cd frontend
  4) Verify npm is correctly installed to path by running the following 3 commands one after another
  > node -v
  > npm -v
  > npx -v
  5) Install packages defined in packages.json with the following command
  > npm install
  6) Verify the environment is working by running the server with the following command
  > npm run dev
  5) This should have run the backend server, access it by visiting 'http://127.0.0.1:5173/' in your browser
  You should see the default react landing page
  **This is a development server, never expose it to a public port**

DEBUGGING ERRORS:
  There may well be problems with this setup I'm not perfect, I'll list common errors below:
  1) Venv activate script system denied permission - you need to change scripting permissions in powershell - google it or let me know and I can fix it
  2) File not found - make sure you are in the right directory, at the start steps 2 and 3 there are instructions to cd to backend for step 2 and fronted for step 3
  3) Can't find node/npm/npx - Node.js installer can sometimes be weird, you need to add the directory to the system path variable
   - open file explorer and go to 'C:\Program Files\nodejs' - if this fails let me know
   - if not go to windows start menu and search 'environment variables'
   - click on the program that pops up
   - click 'advanced'
   - click 'Environment Variables'
   - click 'Path' in the list of variables for user <your name>
   - click 'edit' - DO NOT CLICK NEW
   - click 'new' in the popup
   - paste 'C:\Program Files\nodejs'
   - press ok and close the program
   - restart all vscode windows and terminals then restart the guide at verifying the installation of Node.js - if this fails let me know

Any other errors you can google or let me know, don't force push something to github if you're unsure you've configured it correctly, it could break
 
Now you have fully installed and created the development environment, after any code changes you can run the server to make sure it doesn't break,
and use the testing suites in each app to test functionality. to run the backend server after editing it you need to run the following commands:
> python manage.py makemigrations
> python manage.py migrate
> python manage.py runserver

To run the backend you simply use the following command
> npm run dev

